 "drivingQuestion": "From where is it derived that wisdom overrides lineage?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav Aḥa b. R. Ḥanina supplies the verse.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "horayot.13a.20",
   "daf": "13a",
   "sentenceId": 19,
   "he": "אֵימָתַי? בִּזְמַן שֶׁכּוּלָּן שָׁוִין כּוּ׳. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? אָמַר רַב אַחָא בְּרַבִּי חֲנִינָא, דְּאָמַר קְרָא: ״יְקָרָה הִיא מִפְּנִינִים״, מִכֹּהֵן גָּדוֹל שֶׁנִּכְנָס לִפְנַי וְלִפְנִים.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «When» do these halakhot of precedence take effect? In circumstances «when they are all equal» in terms of wisdom. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters» derived? «Rav Aḥa, son of Rabbi Ḥanina, said:» This is derived from a verse, «as the verse states: “She is more precious than rubies [mipeninim]”» (Proverbs 3:15). The Torah is more precious «than» the «High Priest who enters the innermost sanctum [lifnai velifnim],» the Holy of Holies."
  }
 ],
